-- title:
--   Strict transforms detected on the Deligne–Rapoport closed fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a Deligne–Rapoport model package $\mathfrak X$ for $p$ (so in particular the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb Z$ together with its auxiliary data), a discrete valuation ring $O$ which is a domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$, a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$, and a resolved model package $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}$ for these data, with total space $Y$, structure morphism $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toBase} : Y \to \operatorname{Spec} O$, proper morphism $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toDR}$ from $Y$ to the base change of `DRModel p` along $\mathbb Z \to O$, a finite set of nodes with widths, and ideal sheaf data $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{comp}\,v$ indexed by $v$ in $\mathrm{Fin}\,2 \sqcup \coprod_n \mathrm{Fin}(\mathrm{width}(n)-1)$. Let $t$ be a section of $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toBase}$, that is, a morphism $t_1 : \operatorname{Spec} O \to Y$ with $t_1$ followed by the structure morphism equal to the identity, and let $c$ be an index such that the image of the closed point of $O$ under $t_1$ lies in the support of $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{comp}\,c$ and in the support of no $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{comp}\,w$ for $w \neq c$. Write $t'$ for the image of the closed point of $O$ under $t_1$ followed by $\mathfrak X^{\mathrm{reg}}.\mathrm{toDR}$. Then $c$ is the first element $\mathrm{inl}\,0$ of $\mathrm{Fin}\,2$ if and only if $t'$ lies in the range of the map on points of $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ` and not in the range of the corresponding map for $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa$; and $c = \mathrm{inl}\,1$ if and only if the two conditions are interchanged.
--
--   This identifies, for a section of the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model over $O$ meeting exactly one component of the closed fibre, when that component is one of the two strict transforms of the branches of the Deligne–Rapoport fibre: the answer is read off from which of the two distinguished subschemes $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$, $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa$ contains the image point, the criterion for lying in the smooth locus being supplied by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.mem_preimage_smoothLocus_iff_not_mem_range_compInf_inter_range_compZero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.mem_preimage_smoothLocus_iff_not_mem_range_compInf_inter_range_compZero) (for an exceptional index $c$ the image is a crossing point, lying on both branches, so both right-hand sides fail). It is used in the construction of the dictionary between nodes and components of the resolved fibre attached to a pair of sections.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_DRResolvedModelPackage_eq_inl_iff_toDR_base_mem_range_compInf_of_mem_comp_support.lean

